{"cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/japanese-chinese-cuisine","n":"Japanese Chinese cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Diaspora cuisine in Japan","intro":[["Japanese Chinese cuisine, known as chūka ryōri or simply chūka, refers to Japanese-style Chinese dishes and the restaurants in Japan that serve them. It represents a unique fusion of Japanese and Chinese culinary traditions that have evolved since the late 19th century. This style of food is considered distinct from the \"authentic Chinese food\" available in Japan, though it retains strong influences from various Chinese regional cuisines, and there is considerable overlap between the two."],["A significant number of these dishes were introduced to Japan either by Chinese immigrants or Japanese colonizers returning from the Second Sino-Japanese war in China. This style of cuisine has found its expression in three main types of restaurants: ramen restaurants, dim sum houses, and standard Chinese-style restaurants. Most Japanese Chinese dishes have roots in Cantonese cuisine. Adaptations of Sichuanese cuisine were first introduced to Japan by celebrity chef Chen Kenmin."],["The shippoku culinary style of Nagasaki is heavily influenced by Chinese cuisine, but it is not classified as Japanese Chinese cuisine, as it originated in the 17th century, predating the development of modern Japanese Chinese cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"japanese-chinese-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_Chinese_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":3,"rows":[{"name":"Sudachi Recipes: Wafu Pasta","ref":"site/sudachirecipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"sudachirecipes.com","note":"Chuka recipes such as gyoza, ebi mayo and tantanmen from Japanese cook Yuto Omura.","url":"https://sudachirecipes.com/chuka-ryori-recipes/","suggested":true},{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's collection of chuka dishes as cooked in Japanese homes.","url":"https://www.justonecookbook.com/japanese-chinese-food-recipes/","suggested":true},{"name":"No Recipes: Japanese Chinese","ref":"site/norecipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"norecipes.com","note":"Japanese Chinese recipe category on Marc Matsumoto's food site.","url":"https://norecipes.com/recipe/cuisine/japanese-chinese/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":3,"links":[["Chahan (dish)","dish/chahan-dish"],["Narutomaki","dish/narutomaki"],["Ramen shop","dish/ramen-shop"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Surimi","ingredient/surimi"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Japanese Chinese cooking","count":1,"links":[["Shippoku","cuisine/shippoku"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/60/%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%A1%E3%83%B3%E5%A4%A7%E5%B0%86%E5%9B%9E%E9%8D%8B%E8%82%89%E5%AE%9A%E9%A3%9F.jpg/500px-%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%A1%E3%83%B3%E5%A4%A7%E5%B0%86%E5%9B%9E%E9%8D%8B%E8%82%89%E5%AE%9A%E9%A3%9F.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"ノボホショコロトソ","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%A1%E3%83%B3%E5%A4%A7%E5%B0%86%E5%9B%9E%E9%8D%8B%E8%82%89%E5%AE%9A%E9%A3%9F.jpg"}},"cuisine/list-of-sino-mauritian-dishes":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/list-of-sino-mauritian-dishes","n":"Mauritian Chinese cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[["This is a list of Chinese and Chinese-influenced dishes in Sino-Mauritian cuisine:"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"list-of-sino-mauritian-dishes"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Sino-Mauritian_dishes"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"cuisine/faroese-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/faroese-cuisine","n":"Faroese cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Danish cuisine","cuisine/danish-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Denmark","intro":[["Important parts of Faroese cuisine are lamb and also fish owing to proximity to the sea. Traditional foods from the Faroe Islands include skerpikjøt (a type of dried mutton), seafood, whale meat, blubber, garnatálg, Atlantic puffins, potatoes, and few fresh vegetables."],["Much of the taste of this traditional country food is determined by the food preservation methods used; brine, drying, and the maturing of meat and fish, called ræstkjøt and ræstur fiskur."],["Animal products dominate Faroese cuisine. Popular taste has developed, however, to become closer to the European norm, and consumption of vegetables has greatly increased in recent decades while consumption of fish has diminished. Fresh and ræst lamb meat remains very popular while traditional meat products, such as various types of sausages, have lost much of their appeal with younger generations."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"faroese-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faroese_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Danish cuisine","cuisine/danish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Koks: Faroe Islands Flavour","ref":"cookbook/koks-faroe-islands-flavour","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Poul Andrias Ziska, Tim Ecott","note":"Book from the Faroese restaurant Koks on traditional Faroese ingredients and techniques.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Danish cuisine","cuisine/danish-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6a/Tvost_og_spik.jpg/500px-Tvost_og_spik.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"Arne List","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tvost_og_spik.jpg"}},"dish/casa-vega":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/casa-vega","n":"Casa Vega","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Mexican cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Casa Vega is a restaurant in Sherman Oaks, California. In 2022 it was named one of America's Classics by the James Beard Foundation."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-casa-vega"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casa_Vega"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","ref":"site/mexicoinmykitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.com","note":"Mely Martínez's long-running blog of Mexican home-style recipes.","url":"https://www.mexicoinmykitchen.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Pati Jinich","ref":"site/patijinich-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"patijinich.com","note":"Recipe archive from the Mexican-born chef and host of the PBS series Pati's Mexican Table.","url":"https://patijinich.com/recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Mexican cuisine","links":[["Acapulco Mexican Restaurant and Cantina","dish/acapulco-mexican-restaurant-and-cantina"],["Amigos (restaurant chain)","dish/amigos-restaurant-chain"],["Animalón","dish/animalon"],["Anna's Taqueria","dish/anna-s-taqueria"],["Baker's Drive-Thru","dish/baker-s-drive-thru"],["Barburrito","dish/barburrito"],["Birrieria La Plaza","dish/birrieria-la-plaza"],["Birrieria PDX","dish/birrieria-pdx"],["Boca Grande Taqueria","dish/boca-grande-taqueria"],["BurritoVil