specially Finland, Latvia, Lithuania, Sweden, Russia and Estonia, and in some lakes of Norway, the United Kingdom, northern Germany, and Poland. It is also found in diluted brackish water in the Gulfs of Finland and Bothnia, both of which are in the Baltic Sea."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-coregonus-albula"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coregonus_albula"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Finnish cuisine","cuisine/finnish-cuisine",[["Kalakukko","dish/kalakukko"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["European perch","ingredient/european-perch"],["Fish fillet","ingredient/fish-fillet"],["Pork belly","ingredient/pork-belly"],["Rye flour","ingredient/rye-flour"],["Salmon","ingredient/salmon"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/5b/Finnish_fried_vendace_%28Paistetut_muikut%29.jpg/500px-Finnish_fried_vendace_%28Paistetut_muikut%29.jpg","w":500,"h":332,"by":"V-7","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finnish_fried_vendace_(Paistetut_muikut).jpg"}},"ingredient/agaricus-bisporus":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/agaricus-bisporus","n":"Agaricus bisporus","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 5 dishes across 5 cuisines","intro":[["Agaricus bisporus, the cultivated mushroom, is a basidiomycete mushroom native to grasslands in Eurasia and North America. It is cultivated in more than 70 countries and is one of the most commonly and widely consumed mushrooms in the world. It has two color states while immature – white and brown – both of which have various names, with additional names for the mature state, such as chestnut, portobello, portabellini, button, cremini, and champignon de Paris (see Names below)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-agaricus-bisporus"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agaricus_bisporus"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":5,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Mie ayam","dish/mie-ayam"]]],["Korean Chinese cuisine","cuisine/korean-chinese-cuisine",[["Ulmyeon","dish/ulmyeon"]]],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine",[["Zapiekanka","dish/zapiekanka"]]],["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Tom kha kai","dish/tom-kha-kai"]]],["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku",[["Naporitan","dish/naporitan"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Noodle","ingredient/noodle"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Ketchup","ingredient/ketchup"],["Chinese cabbage","ingredient/chinese-cabbage"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Scallion","ingredient/scallion"],["Scallions","ingredient/scallions"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Sweet soy sauce","ingredient/sweet-soy-sauce"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"],["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/01/ChampignonMushroom.jpg/500px-ChampignonMushroom.jpg","w":500,"h":356,"by":"chris_73","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChampignonMushroom.jpg"}},"dish/nori":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/nori","n":"Nori","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Nori is a dried edible seaweed used in Japanese cuisine, usually made from species of the red algae genus Pyropia, including P. yezoensis and P. tenera. It has a strong and distinctive flavor, and is generally made into flat sheets and used to wrap rolls of sushi or onigiri (rice balls)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-nori"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nori"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisin